error[E1001]: `b.data` is used here after its value moved away
 --> mem:///main.lu:6:13
  |
5 |     let n = consume(take b)
  |                          - `b` moved here
6 |     let m = b.data
  |             ^^^^^^ used after the move
  |
  = note: `b.data` is part of `b`; moving one empties the other. Disjoint fields stay usable.
  = note: re-initializing the place (assigning to it) also makes it usable again.
help: to keep the original, copy it at the move
  |
5 |     let n = consume(take copy b)
  |
